A destroy zeroes a waiting thread but leaves it on a notification that survives.
The ring would lead into memory that is no longer a thread;
a notification queues only live threads.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: queue holds something that is not a thread
Report: queue is not linked back

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -495,9 +495,7 @@ bool sched_forget(struct obj_header *o, bool preempt)
          * Its units went as a node it holds, and with them its place on its queue.
          */
         struct thread *t = (struct thread *)o;
-        if (t->state == THREAD_WAITING) {
-            unwait(t);
-        }
+        (void)t;
         break;
